  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0017","literal","Those holding the noble rank of Fifth Grandee, officials of six hundred piculs and above, and eunuchs who served the emperor and were known by name, if guilty of crimes deserving shackles for theft, were all pardoned and released.","Holders of the noble rank of Fifth Grandee, officials at six hundred bushels or above, and named palace attendants who served the emperor, if guilty of crimes that would ordinarily require fettered custody, were all to be held under privileged restraint instead.","The Chinese term 頌繫 (songxi) means held under privileged/lax restraint without shackles, not 'pardoned and released'. Also 宦皇帝 here refers to serving the emperor, not eunuchs specifically.","high","applied"],
    ["s0018","literal","Grand builders and above and inner and outer grandsons and grandsons who had crimes deserving punishment and deserving to be city wall pounders were all tattooed to become firewood cutters and rice cleaners.","Those ranked Upper Maker or above, together with imperial grandsons and more distant descendants of both inner and outer branches, if guilty of crimes calling for corporal punishment or labor as wall-builders and grain-pounders, were all to have their sentences commuted to the shaved-head labor penalties of ghost-firewood gatherer or white-grain pounder.","The terms 上造 (Shangzao, rank 2) is translated as Grand builders, 耐 (nai) is shaving sides of hair (commutation of corporal punishment), not tattooed. The literal text misidentifies ranks and penalties.","high","applied"],
    ["s0027","literal","In the second year, winter, tenth month, King Dao Hui of Qi came to court and presented Chengyang commandery to increase the fief of Princess Yuan of Lu, honoring the princess as grand empress dowager.","In the second year, winter, tenth month, King Daohui of Qi came to court and presented Chengyang Commandery to enlarge the fief of Princess Yuan of Lu, honoring the princess as queen dowager.","The literal text translates 太后 as grand empress dowager instead of queen dowager for Princess Yuan of Lu.","high","applied"],
    ["s0032","idiomatic","In autumn, seventh month, on the day xinhai, Chancellor He passed away.","In autumn, seventh month, on the day xinwei, Chancellor He passed away.","The source day is 辛未 (xinwei), not 辛亥 (xinhai).","high","applied"],
    ["s0032","literal","In autumn, seventh month, on the day xinhai, Chancellor He passed away.","In autumn, seventh month, on the day xinwei, Chancellor He passed away.","The source day is 辛未 (xinwei), not 辛亥 (xinhai).","high","applied"],
    ["s0041","idiomatic","In the third month on the day jiashen, the emperor was capped. He pardoned the world.","In the third month on the day jiazi, the emperor was capped. He pardoned the world.","The source day is 甲子 (jiazi), not 甲申 (jiashen).","high","applied"],
    ["s0041","literal","In the third month on the day jiashen, the emperor was capped. He pardoned the world.","In the third month on the day jiazi, the emperor was capped. He pardoned the world.","The source day is 甲子 (jiazi), not 甲申 (jiashen).","high","applied"],
    ["s0048","idiomatic","In the fifth year, winter, tenth month, it frosted.","In the fifth year, winter, tenth month, there was thunder.","The received text reads 靁, a variant of 雷 (thunder), not frost; the prior source character 剨 and translation were corrupt.","high","applied"],
    ["s0048","literal","In the fifth year, winter, tenth month, it frosted.","In the fifth year, winter, tenth month, there was thunder.","The received text reads 靁, a variant of 雷 (thunder), not frost; the prior source character 剨 and translation were corrupt.","high","applied"]
